ADC_Keywords: Active gal. nuclei ; Radio sources ; Morphology
Keywords: Galaxies: active - Radio continuum: galaxies -
          Techniques: image processing - Methods: data analysis -
          Methods: statistical

Abstract:
    FIRST-2060 is a four-class labelled dataset of 2060 radio-loud active
    galactic nuclei (RAGNs) built from three publicly available catalogues
    through multi-tier visual inspection. Each source is labelled as a
    straight Fanaroff-Riley type I (sfri) or type II (sfrii), a wide-angle
    tail (wat), or a narrow-angle tail (nat). All sources are drawn from the
    VLA FIRST survey.

Description:
    This table (Table B.1 in the paper) lists all 2060 sources of the
    FIRST-2060 catalogue with their FIRST radio designation, J2000 equatorial
    coordinates and morphological class. The prefix letter of the identifier
    indicates the source catalogue of origin: 'S' for Sasmal et al., 'L' for
    Lao et al., and 'M' for MiraBest. The coordinates (J2000) are those
    encoded in the FIRST radio designation.

